Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-19372) StreamsGroup should not be
 subscribed to a topic when it is empty
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Lucas Brutschy created KAFKA-19372:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: StreamsGroup should not be subscribed to a topic when=
 it is empty
                 Key: KAFKA-19372
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19372
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
            Reporter: Lucas Brutschy


We should behave more like a consumer group and make sure to not be subscri=
bed to the input topics anymore when the last member leaves the group. We d=
on't do this right now because our topology is still initialized even after=
 the last member leaves the group.=20
This will allow:
=C2=A0- Offsets to expire and be cleaned up.
=C2=A0- Offsets to be deleted through admin API calls.
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
=C2=A0



--
