Jun Rao resolved KAFKA-19325.
-----------------------------
    Resolution: Won't Fix

It seems that changing forceComplete() to return void makes the usage less =
convenient.

> improve forceComplete() in DelayedOperation
> -------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-19325
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19325
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Improvement
>          Components: core
>    Affects Versions: 4.1.0
>            Reporter: Jun Rao
>            Assignee: =E9=BB=83=E7=AB=A3=E9=99=BD
>            Priority: Major
>
> After [https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/19759/files,] DelayedOperatio=
n.forceComplete() always returns true when called inside tryComplete(). Onl=
y the expiration logic checks the return value of forceComplete(). We could=
 do the following in the expiration logic and change forceComplete() to ret=
urn void and avoid using the lock there (the caller will get the lock inste=
ad). This simplifies the caller to forceComplete().
> {code:java}
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 lock.lock();
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 try {
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 if (!isCompleted()) {
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 forceComplete();
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 onExpiration();
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0}
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 } finally {
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 lock.unlock();
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 }{code}



