Hi All,

I'm building a custom Docker image for kafka Connect and planning to run it=
 on Kubernetes. I'm a bit stuck on whether I should use a Deployment or a S=
tatefulSet.

>From what I understand, the main difference that could affect Kafka Connect=
 is the hostname/IP behaviour. With a Deployment, pod IPs and hostnames can=
 change after restarts. With a StatefulSet, each pod gets a stable hostname=
 (like connect-0, connect-1, etc.)

My question is: Does it really matter for Kafka Connect(task reassignment) =
if the pod IPs/hostnames(this will be the worker_Id as well) change on rest=
arts, considering its a stateless application?

Thanks

--_000_AS5PR07MB9772B0033A38461A12752A7E9276AAS5PR07MB9772eurp_--

