Jos=C3=A9 Armando Garc=C3=ADa Sancio resolved KAFKA-18751.
------------------------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

> Complete delayed FETCH request when HWM is increased.
> -----------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-18751
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18751
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Improvement
>          Components: kraft
>            Reporter: Jos=C3=A9 Armando Garc=C3=ADa Sancio
>            Assignee: Jos=C3=A9 Armando Garc=C3=ADa Sancio
>            Priority: Major
>             Fix For: 4.1.0
>
>
> It is possible for HWM propagation to get delayed if the the HWM is incre=
ased and there are no new data in the log.
> One solution to this problem is for the leader to track the last HWM sent=
 to the replicas and immediately reply to FETCH request if the HWM is great=
er than the previously sent HWM.
> =C2=A0
> One issue with this solution is that the leader doesn't have a reliable w=
ay of determining that an empty FETCH response made it to the remote replic=
a. This can be address if the FETCH request also include the remotes replic=
a HWM.
> =C2=A0
> =C2=A0



