    Resolution: Fixed

> Client side changes to enable 2PC
> ---------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-19082
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19082
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Sub-task
>            Reporter: Ritika Reddy
>            Assignee: Ritika Reddy
>            Priority: Major
>
> h2. KafkaProducer API Changes
> New=C2=A0{{KafkaProducer.PreparedTxnState}}=C2=A0class is going to be def=
ined as following:
> {panel}
> {panel}
> |{{static}}=C2=A0{{public}}=C2=A0{{class}}=C2=A0{{PreparedTxnState {}}
> {{=C2=A0=C2=A0}}{{public}}=C2=A0{{String toString();}}
> {{=C2=A0=C2=A0}}{{public}}=C2=A0{{PreparedTxnState(String serializedState=
);}}
> {{=C2=A0=C2=A0}}{{public}}=C2=A0{{PreparedTxnState();}}
> {{}}}|
> The objects of this class can serialize to / deserialize from a string va=
lue and can be written to / read from a database.=C2=A0 The implementation =
is going to store=C2=A0{{producerId}}=C2=A0and=C2=A0{{{}epoch{}}}.
> New overloaded method will be added to=C2=A0{{{}KafkaProducer{}}}:
> {{public void initTransactions(boolean keepPreparedTxn)}}=C2=A0
> If the value is 'true' then the corresponding field is set in the=C2=A0{{=
InitProducerIdRequest}}=C2=A0and the=C2=A0{{KafkaProducer}}=C2=A0object is =
set into a state which only allows calling=C2=A0=C2=A0{{{}.commitTransactio=
n{}}},=C2=A0{{.abortTransaction,}}=C2=A0or=C2=A0{{.completeTransaction.}}
> New method will be added to=C2=A0{{{}KafkaProducer{}}}:
> {{public PreparedTxnState prepareTransaction()}}=C2=A0
> This would flush all the pending messages and transition the producer int=
o a mode where only=C2=A0{{{}.commitTransaction{}}},=C2=A0{{.abortTransacti=
on,}}=C2=A0or=C2=A0{{.completeTransaction}}=C2=A0could be called (calling o=
ther methods,=C2=A0 e.g.=C2=A0{{.send}}=C2=A0, in that mode would result in=
=C2=A0{{IllegalStateException}}=C2=A0being thrown).=C2=A0 If the call is su=
ccessful (all messages successfully got flushed to all partitions) the tran=
saction is prepared.=C2=A0 If the 2PC is not enabled, we return the=C2=A0{{=
INVALID_TXN_STATE}}=C2=A0error.
> New method would be added to=C2=A0{{{}KafkaProducer{}}}:
> {{public void completeTransaction(PreparedTxnState preparedTxnState)}}
> The method would compare the currently prepared transaction state and the=
 state passed in the argument and either commit or abort the transaction.=
=C2=A0 If the producer is not in prepared state (i.e. neither prepareTransa=
ction was called nor initTransaction(true) was called) we return an INVALID=
_TXN_STATE error.
> h2. Client Configuration Changes
> *transaction.two.phase.commit.enable*=C2=A0The default would be =E2=80=98=
false=E2=80=99.=C2=A0 If set to =E2=80=98true=E2=80=99, then the broker is =
informed that the client is participating in two phase commit protocol and =
transactions that this client starts never expire.
> *transaction.timeout.ms*=C2=A0The semantics is not changed, but it would =
be an error to set=C2=A0*transaction.timeout.ms*=C2=A0when=C2=A0*two.phase.=
commit.enable*=C2=A0is set to 'true=E2=80=99.
