Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-19434) Move logic for for state store
 initiation to StreamThread handover
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Bill Bejeck created KAFKA-19434:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Move logic for for state store initiation to StreamTh=
read handover
                 Key: KAFKA-19434
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19434
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Task
          Components: streams
            Reporter: Bill Bejeck
            Assignee: Bill Bejeck
             Fix For: 4.2.0


When starting a Kafka Streams instance, if it has pre-existing state, the
state stores are initialized on the main thread. Part of this
initialization registers the stateful metrics with the JMX thread-id tag
of=C2=A0{{{}main{}}}. This breaks the KIP-1076 implementation where need to
register metrics with thread-id tags of=C2=A0{{{}xxxStreamThread-N{}}}. Thi=
s is
necessary due to the fact that the=C2=A0{{StreamsMetric}}=C2=A0is a singlet=
on shared
by all=C2=A0{{StreamThread}}=C2=A0instances, so we need to make sure only a=
dd
metrics for the current=C2=A0{{StreamThread}}=C2=A0otherwise duplicate metr=
ics are
registered.=C2=A0 So the task is to move state store initialization to the =
point when the main thread hands the store over to the assigned `StreamThre=
ad`



--
