Dear Kafka Developers,

My name is *Surafel Temesgen*, and I=E2=80=99d like to introduce you to a p=
roject
I=E2=80=99ve been building called *Debo*=E2=80=94an open-source, desktop-ba=
sed
infrastructure management tool designed to provide unified control and
monitoring across components in the Hadoop ecosystem, including *Apache
Kafka*.
------------------------------
=F0=9F=92=A1 What is Debo?

*Debo* is a lightweight application (written in C) that acts as a
centralized management interface for distributed systems. It supports:

   -

   *Kafka*, *Zookeeper*, *HDFS*, *YARN*
   -

   *Flink*, *Spark*, *Hive*, *HBase*
   -

   And other components like Atlas, Ranger, Tez, Hue, Oozie, Pig, Presto,
   Phoenix, etc.

The idea is to reduce operational overhead by giving users a single
interface to monitor status and control services like Kafka clusters,
brokers, and optionally, consumers or topics.
------------------------------
=F0=9F=9A=80 Incubator Proposal & Community Feedback

Debo has been proposed to the Apache Incubator and is currently in need of =
*3
PMC sponsors* to proceed. I welcome your feedback and support on the
discussion thread here:
=F0=9F=94=97 https://lists.apache.org/thread/bp0rqvf4xvmdb3n1m2fzhwym95841s=
5v

Despite not being incubated yet, I plan to *release a beta version in the
coming weeks*, including Kafka-related functionality and usage instructions=
.
------------------------------
=F0=9F=99=8F Call for Kafka-Specific Feedback

I=E2=80=99m particularly interested in Kafka developers' thoughts on:

   -

   What Kafka management features are most valuable in a lightweight tool
   like Debo
   -

   Ideas for interacting with brokers, topics, or monitoring consumers
   -

   Possible feature requests for debugging or lightweight control operation=
s

------------------------------
=F0=9F=93=BA Learn More

I=E2=80=99ve set up a YouTube channel where I=E2=80=99ll post video tutoria=
ls and
walkthroughs:
=F0=9F=91=89 https://www.youtube.com/@Debo_teamwork

You can also explore the source code and follow development here:
